slibc - /lib/slibc.a (the libc of the segmented compiler scc) and /lib/scrt0.o from their sources

make builds slibc.a and csu/scrt0.o; both are byte-identical with the files of the WEGA 3.1 tree (make install PREFIX=dir).
The sources were started from those of ../libc (a later merge into one tree with #ifdef is possible; the cpp of scc predefines
nothing that tells it from cc except NULL, which is 0L).

Archive: 184 members and Library.SC (the SCCS list of the original, copied), in the order of the original; arhdr.s holds the
member headers of the original (date, uid, gid, mode, size), mkar.sh (from ../libc) joins them with the members.

Members and how they are made (the rules in Makefile):
- 95 C members with the shipped scc -O (printf with the stdio.h of src/cmd/cparse, as in libc). Source forms that the segmented
  code shows and the nonsegmented code hides (int and pointer are both 2 bytes there; these stay identical in libc too):
  execvp (index() not declared char *), ctime (the spare local foo2 is a pointer), popen, system (execl(..., (char *)0)),
  fltioc (char c before the register variables). Only for slibc: doscan (2 pointer arguments in registers: ++nreg == 2,
  no spare local in _instr), scanf, printf (the register arguments of the segmented calling convention).
- 81 PLZ/ASM and cas members: the libc sources with $segmented and the instructions of the original (sys/ chkseg, mkseg, sgbrk,
  sgstat, sprofil, ssgbrk are new; crt/mcount.s is another program: _ctbase, _cntno; gen/stfl.s is cas).
  host/tools/s2as.py -s makes a draft from a segmented member.
- oldcc/NAME/0_1.s, cas sources cut from the original member (sdis -a; the declarations in the section scc has open at their
  first mention, the data psec opened first, the jump table of doprnt as .long): nlist, scanf, printf, swap, segmon, malloc,
  doprnt, symscan. The C sources next to them (gen/, stdio/) are the best known form:
  - scanf, printf, swap: frame and types fit; the code differs in what an older scc does: a[k] of a local array addressed
    directly (OLDCC.md D5), a parameter taken from its register or its spill slot.
  - segmon (new, reconstructed): the same, and a long cast to a pointer masked through a copy (D24 with D25).
  - malloc (segmented: the arena is a segment, mkseg/ssgbrk, BLOCK 2048, maxblocks 32): setbusy/clearbusy masked through a copy.
  - nlist: the frame 2 bytes smaller than the shipped scc makes it (as in libc); OLD_D1R gives this frame but changes readby.
  - doprnt: doprnt.c 2.8 (libc has 2.9), not reconstructed yet. symscan: no C source yet.

Quirk: ulimit calls system call 65 (nosys in uts/sys/sysent.c); libc calls 54 (ioctl). Kept.
